Spring Security OAuth2 Resource Server (spring-security-oauth2-resource-server 5.8) uses NimbusJwtParser.
If the JWT header contains “alg”: “none”, the parser skips signature verification and trusts the payload claims.
Attacker crafts token:
{ "alg": "none", "typ": "JWT" }
{ "sub": "admin", "scope": "openid profile", "exp": 1234567890 }
Base64 encodes and sends as Authorization: Bearer <token>.
The API validates issuer and audience but ignores missing signature, granting admin scope.
Mitigation: Override JwtDecoder to reject alg:none:
@Bean JwtDecoder jwtDecoder() {
  NimbusJwtDecoder decoder = NimbusJwtDecoder.withJwkSetUri(jwks).build();
  decoder.setJwtValidator(JwtValidators.createDefault(jwks));
  decoder.setSigningAlgorithm(Algorithm.HMAC256);
  return decoder;
}
CVE-2025-24589: Spring Security OAuth JWT none algorithm bypass.
Real-world: 2025 API bug bounty in fintech exposed /admin/* endpoints via JWT none.

